        // NEW: mean-residual anchoring — a fresh bin is only cheap to open when
        // its post-residual is at or below the mean residual (i.e., the leftover
        // is at least as tight as the average bin's slack). Overshooting the
        // mean residual creates a fatter, less usable leftover than the fleet
        // average and should be penalized proportionally.
